{#
    The standing "your notifications are off" reminder — two flavours, one bar
    slot, always at least one of them possible.

    `partials/push-prompt.twig` is a one-off *offer*: it is dismissible, it is
    quiet for a fortnight afterwards, and it disappears the moment permission
    is answered. That is the right shape for a first ask and the wrong shape
    for someone who has already decided — switched push off in /profile, or
    told the browser "no" and then never heard anything again. This partial is
    what replaces it: no dismissal, no expiry, rendering on every authenticated
    page until notifications actually work here.

    The two cases are split by who can know about them:

      - `push_enabled = 0` is an *account* fact, so the server renders that bar
        visible. It survives a dismissal, a 14-day window and a second
        browser — none of which are things the client can be trusted to
        remember consistently.
      - `Notification.permission === 'denied'` is a *browser* fact the server
        has no way to see, so that bar ships `hidden` and `push-prompt.js`
        (`revealDeniedReminder()`) unhides it only when the browser has
        actually refused. Rendered visible it would nag people whose
        permission is fine; not rendered at all it would never reach the one
        person it is for — the visitor we can never ask again.

    They are mutually exclusive by construction: the account bar takes the
    `push_enabled = 0` branch, the denied bar the `else`. Two bars about the
    same broken pipe would be noise, and the account switch is the first thing
    to fix anyway.

    Two further asymmetries, shared by both bars:

      - Not dismissible. A reminder that can be dismissed is a prompt, and the
        prompt already exists. What is missing is the *nagging*, which is the
        whole point: push is off by default for a new account, and a person
        who never learns that their order finished never finds out.
      - It does not render on `/profile` or `/app`, the two pages that carry
        the switch itself. Telling someone to go and do the thing on the page
        where they are already standing is noise. The denied bar has no link
        at all, because a browser refusal is fixed in the browser's own site
        settings — there is no page here that can undo it.

    It is also in-flow rather than a fixed overlay, so "permanent" costs a
    single line at the top of the page instead of the bottom of the screen.

    The account switch is read by `IdentityViewInjection` (`pushEnabled`), and
    `vapidEnabled` comes from `PushViewInjection` — a deployment with no keys
    must not be told to turn on notifications it cannot deliver.
#}
{% if identity and vapidEnabled and currentPath not in ['/profile', '/app'] %}
    {% if not pushEnabled %}
        <div class="alert alert-info" role="status" data-push-reminder>
            {{ icon('bell-ring', 'w-5 h-5 shrink-0') }}
            <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                <p class="font-semibold">অ্যাকাউন্ট নোটিফিকেশন বন্ধ আছে</p>
                <p class="text-xs">
                    অর্ডার ও রিচার্জের আপডেট এই ব্রাউজারে আসবে না — অ্যাকাউন্ট সুইচ চালু না করা পর্যন্ত কোনো ব্রাউজারেই পাঠানো হবে না।
                </p>
            </div>
            <a href="/profile" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm shrink-0">সেটিংসে যান</a>
        </div>
    {% else %}
        {# Hidden until `revealDeniedReminder()` confirms the browser said no:
           the server cannot know, and a bar shown to everyone is a bar people
           stop reading. The `hidden` attribute is pinned by `.alert[hidden]`
           in app.css — preflight's `[hidden]` loses to `.alert`'s
           display:flex on equal specificity. #}
        <div class="alert alert-warning" role="status" data-push-denied hidden>
            {{ icon('bell-ring', 'w-5 h-5 shrink-0') }}
            <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                <p class="font-semibold">ব্রাউজারে নোটিফিকেশন বন্ধ আছে</p>
                <p class="text-xs">
                    এই ব্রাউজারে অর্ডার ও রিচার্জের আপডেট আসবে না — ব্রাউজারের সাইট সেটিংস থেকে নোটিফিকেশনের অনুমতি দিন।
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
{% endif %}
